ble","scoringCurrency":null,"applicability":"financialSector","checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:43:41.900Z","evidenceHash":"685df053b39206da10f22c38f829f3e3c183fb3110d164d4bb668e3d0f57a23f"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":null,"period":null,"basis":null,"model":null,"zone":null,"reason":"financialSectorNotApplicable","scoringCurrency":null,"applicability":"financialSector","checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:43:41.900Z","evidenceHash":"685df053b39206da10f22c38f829f3e3c183fb3110d164d4bb668e3d0f57a23f"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":true,"reference":{"date":"2026-09-30","label":"FY 2026 Q3","period":"quarterly","flow":"ttm","balance":"beginning","rote":349.45606694560666,"warnings":[],"tbvps":25.338717655446413,"reason":null},"rote":349.45606694560666,"tbvps":25.338717655446413,"bvps":25.338717655446413,"g":2.25,"dps_total":1.3630587885401737,"dps_source":"ttmQuarterly","dps_source_date":"2026-09-30","pb_tangible":2.1883506795412493,"ke_floor_pct":9,"ke_floor_applied":true,"ke_capm":8.1475,"ke":9,"excess_return_fair":1303.37,"ddm_fair":24.75},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CNO.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CNO.png","website":"https://www.cnoinc.com","ceo":"Gary C. Bhojwani","full_time_employees":"3300","description":"Headquartered in Carmel, Indiana, and established in 1979, CNO Financial Group, Inc. operates across the United States, developing, marketing, and administering a broad spectrum of insurance and annuity products primarily for middle-income and senior individuals. The company's health insurance offerings span Medicare supplement plans, various supplemental health coverage (such as specified disease, accident, and hospital indemnity products), long-term care policies, and Medicare Advantage plans. CNO also underwrites a full suite of life insurance products, encompassing universal life, interest-sensitive options, and traditional policies like whole life, graded benefit life, term life, and single premium whole life. For wealth accumulation and retirement income, CNO provides an array of annuities, including fixed index, fixed interest (single and flexible premium deferred), and single premium immediate annuities, often catering to retirees and older self-employed individuals within the middle-income demographic. CNO employs a multi-channel approach to reach its diverse clientele. Individual customers can access products directly through phone, online platforms, mail, or face-to-face interactions. Additionally, the firm cultivates relationships with businesses, associations, and other membership groups, facilitating worksite and group sales by engaging with potential clients at their workplaces. These offerings are distributed through a robust network of agents, independent producers, and direct marketing efforts, promoted under the well-recognized brand names of Bankers Life, Washington National, and Colonial Penn.","description_en":"Headquartered in Carmel, Indiana, and established in 1979, CNO Financial Group, Inc. operates across the United States, developing, marketing, and administering a broad spectrum of insurance and annuity products primarily for middle-income and senior individuals. The company's health insurance offerings span Medicare supplement plans, various supplemental health coverage (such as specified disease, accident, and hospital indemnity products), long-term care policies, and Medicare Advantage plans. CNO also underwrites a full suite of life insurance products, encompassing universal life, interest-sensitive options, and traditional policies like whole life, graded benefit life, term life, and single premium whole life. For wealth accumulation and retirement income, CNO provides an array of annuities, including fixed index, fixed interest (single and flexible premium deferred), and single premium immediate annuities, often catering to retirees and older self-employed individuals within the middle-income demographic. CNO employs a multi-channel approach to reach its diverse clientele. Individual customers can access products directly through phone, online platforms, mail, or face-to-face interactions. Additionally, the firm cultivates relationships with businesses, associations, and other membership groups, facilitating worksite and group sales by engaging with potential clients at their workplaces. These offerings are distributed through a robust network of agents, independent producers, and direct marketing efforts, promoted under the well-recognized brand names of Bankers Life, Washington National, and Colonial Penn.","description_zh":"CNO Financial Group, Inc.（美股代碼：CNO）為 Financial Services 領域之重要企業，專注於 Insurance - Life 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"11299 Illinois Street","city":"Carmel","state":"IN","zip":"46032","country":"US","phone":"317 817 6100","full_address":"11299 Illinois Street, Carmel, IN 46032, US","range_52w":"38.99-59.15","year_high":59.15,"year_low":38.99,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":38.99,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-09-16","name":"Williams Jeremy D.","title":"officer: Chief Actuary","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":4420,"price":21.06,"total_val":0.09},{"date":"2026-09-16","name":"Williams Jeremy D.","title":"officer: Chief Actuary","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":3240,"price":23.33,"total_val":0.08},{"date":"2026-09-16","name":"Williams Jeremy D.","title":"officer: Chief Actuary","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":3240,"price":55.71,"total_val":0.18},{"date":"2026-09-16","name":"Williams Jeremy D.","title":"officer: Chief Actuary","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":4420,"price":55.27,"total_val":0.24},{"date":"2026-09-16","name":"Williams Jeremy D.","title":"officer: Chief Actuary","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1122,"price":55.72,"total_val":0.06},{"date":"2026-09-16","name":"Williams Jeremy D.","title":"officer: Chief Actuary","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":442